#: src/kernel/firecracker.md:1
msgid "Running Asterinas on Firecracker"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/firecracker.md:3
msgid ""
"Asterinas can run as a guest kernel inside a [Firecracker](https://github."
"com/firecracker-microvm/firecracker) microVM through the PVH boot protocol. "
"This page shows how to build the kernel and boot it with Firecracker."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/firecracker.md:8
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/firecracker.md:10
msgid "An x86-64 host with KVM enabled (`/dev/kvm` accessible)."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/firecracker.md:11
msgid ""
"A `firecracker` binary in `PATH`. The Asterinas Docker development image "
"already has Firecracker installed."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/firecracker.md:14
msgid "Build the kernel"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/firecracker.md:20
msgid ""
"This builds a PVH-bootable kernel image. `BOOT_PROTOCOL=pvh` automatically "
"uses the `vmm-direct` boot method and enables the `pvh_boot` feature."
msgstr ""

